{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/7p6gg3","slide":1,"text":"Welcome learners and read the driving question aloud. Ask for a quick show of hands: who has used an AI assistant, who has relied on an automated code-review tool, and who has had to explain why an automated finding was correct? Frame this session as engineering a trustworthy system around model capability. Preview that every claim in the course will be tied to evidence, a contract, a workflow state, or a human authority boundary. Do not teach the whole session from the title slide; use it to establish the problem and invite one concrete experience from the room.\n\n[Sources]\n- Code Review Harness repository: contracts/evidence-contract.md; contracts/contract-dependency-graph.md; contracts/style-and-validation.md"}
